{"name":"Ice Fishing","hex":"#dcecf5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ice fishing","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The practice of fishing through a hole cut in the ice."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of ice fish"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice_fishing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ice fishing","blocks":[{"text":"Ice fishing is the practice of catching fish with lines and fish hooks or spears through an opening in the ice on a frozen body of water. Ice fishers may fish in the open or in heated enclosures, some with bunks and amenities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Ice_fisher_catching_a_fish_NB.jpg/330px-Ice_fisher_catching_a_fish_NB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_fishing","wikidata":"Q1313678"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"},{"title":"Fishing","blocks":[{"text":"Fishing is the activity of trying to catch fish. Fish are often caught as wildlife from the natural environment, but may also be caught from stocked bodies of water such as ponds, canals, park wetlands and reservoirs. Fishing techniques include trawling, longlining, jigging, hand-gathering, spearing, netting, angling, shooting and trapping, as well as more destructive and often illegal techniques such as electrocution, blasting and poisoning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Stilts_fishermen_Sri_Lanka_02.jpg/330px-Stilts_fishermen_Sri_Lanka_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fishing","wikidata":"Q14373"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Winter_fishing_on_the_ice%2C_early_20th.cent._-_Fony%C3%B3d%2C_Hungary.jpg/500px-Winter_fishing_on_the_ice%2C_early_20th.cent._-_Fony%C3%B3d%2C_Hungary.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Winter_fishing_on_the_ice%2C_early_20th.cent._-_Fony%C3%B3d%2C_Hungary.jpg/1280px-Winter_fishing_on_the_ice%2C_early_20th.cent._-_Fony%C3%B3d%2C_Hungary.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Winter_fishing_on_the_ice%2C_early_20th.cent._-_Fony%C3%B3d%2C_Hungary.jpg/500px-Winter_fishing_on_the_ice%2C_early_20th.cent._-_Fony%C3%B3d%2C_Hungary.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Winter ice fishing in Fonyod, Hungary (1910)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWinter_fishing_on_the_ice%2C_early_20th.cent._-_Fony%C3%B3d%2C_Hungary.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Ice_fishing_on_the_Yalu_River.jpg/500px-Ice_fishing_on_the_Yalu_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Ice_fishing_on_the_Yalu_River.jpg/1280px-Ice_fishing_on_the_Yalu_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 